/*! @brief A plain-object dictionary of handler forms, keyed by route pattern

 HandlerMap is the typed form of the routing maps accepted by `mq.Routing`,
 `mq.Handler`, `Chain.append`, `mq.invoke` and the server constructors. It is a
 regular JavaScript object dictionary (not an ES `Map`); keys are match patterns
 and values are handlers.

 A value may be a Handler object, an array of handler forms (converted to a
 Chain), a nested HandlerMap (converted to a nested Routing), a handler function
 or a path/address string. JavaScript handler functions consume the message and
 their return value is ignored.

 Example 1 — a routing map with two handlers:
 ```JavaScript
 const mq = require('mq');

 const app = new mq.Routing({
     '/a': (req) => { },
     '/b': (req) => { }
 });
 console.log(app.isRouting()); // true
 ```

 Example 2 — nested maps and handler arrays:
 ```JavaScript
 const mq = require('mq');

 const app = new mq.Routing({
     '/api': {
         '/users': [
             (req) => { },
             (req) => { }
         ]
     }
 });
 console.log(app.isRouting()); // true
 ```
*/
map HandlerMap: Handler|Array|HandlerMap|String|Function(Value req, ...params) => void;
